{"created": "2026-07-17T19:14:39.840975+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-17T19:15:28.067005+00:00", "id": 21418942, "conceptrecid": "21124403", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21418942", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21124403", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21418942", "metadata": {"title": "Interlanguage and Mathematical Translation Methodology Sidecar (v0.5 Research Method and Automata Audit)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21418942", "publication_date": "2026-07-17", "description": "<p>This version extends the interlanguage and mathematical-translation methodology sidecar with a consolidated research method, evidence and authority rules, an operational decision interface, eight language-lane handoffs, and reproducible audits of the current weighted-automata data.</p><p><strong>Read first:</strong> <code>00_Interlanguage_Research_Method_Current_v05_20260717.pdf</code>. The grouped file <code>12_Interlanguage_Research_Department_and_Automata_v05_20260717.zip</code> contains the complete research-department handoff, exact source archives, extracted CSV/JSON/Markdown data, the executable audit, fresh audit results, manifests, and checksums.</p><p><strong>Reproduced data state:</strong> the Interslavic State C package contains 1,229 ledger rows, 1,215 unique term identifiers, 100 concept buckets, and 9,124 edges. Its W0 result is retained explicitly as a projection only. The unified v6.2 package contains 15 lane rows, 1,522 marker rows, 6,088 edges, and 362 concept rows. Its numerical readiness proxy is reproducible but rejected as a readiness or quality decision measure because candidate mass can produce high scores without accepted witness evidence.</p><p><strong>Operational status:</strong> this package is research method, reproducibility material, routing infrastructure, and manager handoff documentation. It is not native-speaker approval, community acceptance, a finished interlanguage, a completed translation corpus, or mathematical source-fidelity certification. Generated or candidate material remains distinct from independent source witnesses and accepted terminology.</p><p><strong>GitHub:</strong> corrections, additional source bodies, improved weighting methods, and cleaned language-lane packages can be suggested through issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Manuscript Typesetting Project", "affiliation": "Independent"}], "keywords": ["interlanguage", "Interslavic", "constructed languages", "mathematical translation", "weighted automata", "evidence graph", "term ledger", "source provenance", "reproducible audit", "AI-run workflow", "language management", "marginal intelligibility"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.20461174", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.20412587", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "2026-07-17 v0.5 research method and automata audit", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-zero"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 7, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21124403"}}]}, "notes": "v0.5 consolidates the current research method, evidence-governance rules, language-lane handoffs, exact automata data, and executable audit. It does not certify language completion, terminology acceptance, native-speaker approval, translation fidelity, or critical-edition status."}, "title": "Interlanguage and Mathematical Translation Methodology Sidecar (v0.5 Research Method and Automata Audit)", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21418942", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21418942", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21418942?preview=1", "doi": "h